{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T02:21:46.124Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f45252e8e8358ffe097d038b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T02:21:46.124Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Re-review round 1 (auto) posted one non-blocking CodeRabbit finding on test/proof-budget.test.ts:43 — keep the outer watchdog above the nested proof budget at small scales. Verified valid: at a valid explicit PM_TEST_TIME_SCALE of 0.4 the outer testTime(10_000) drops to 4,000 ms while the nested regression needs at least 4,200 ms (1,200 ms within-budget proof plus the child-forced 3x watchdog of 3,000 ms), so the outer execFileSync kills the test although the code is correct; depth validation accepts any finite scale above zero. General rule: a harness watchdog that guards nested proof work whose budget is independent of the outer scale (child-forced scale, self-set V8 coverage, fixed nested sleeps) never scales below its declared unscaled budget."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T02:21:46.124Z"}],"before_hash":"e5371e840b3df501bf52c3dfde77ea3087dcf553332f48b18785810b2c624ee3","after_hash":"66b607fd5bb9ed3ffc75739926e285a925bd704609ea406fa477cc0ac88177ad","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"19f2213317a1a3415a8cb76d482097f41f04692e38fe5ba8522a40bc799f94e3"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T02:21:52.047Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f45252e8e8358ffe097d038b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T02:21:52.046Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Class sweep: the only outer watchdogs around nested independently-budgeted proof children are the two outer execFileSync watchdogs in test/proof-budget.test.ts — line 43 (the flagged one) and the same-shaped line 23, whose nested budget is instrumented child startup (a valid 0.01-scale run gives it 100 ms, below the measured ~130 ms). Product code never reads the harness scale and scripts use fixed unscaled timeouts, so no SDK/CLI instance exists. Must-allow corpus: test/lm-cli.test.ts and test/evaluation-plan.test.ts launch runTimedProof children with no outer scaled watchdog (their children inherit the suite scale), and test/depth.test.ts guards scale-forcing children with a plain unscaled 30,000 ms. Fix: outerProofTime(ms) = Math.max(ms, testTime(ms)) exported from test/support/proof-budget.ts with a docstring, used for both outer watchdogs; higher scales keep the larger budgets, and the two pre-existing tests are unchanged."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T02:21:52.047Z"}],"before_hash":"66b607fd5bb9ed3ffc75739926e285a925bd704609ea406fa477cc0ac88177ad","after_hash":"a2e41fcc088a85943f279d56d8649fd4fd07015818659aa90f48b3fe62195516","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"139b6f2941be4cb57e2cd35b74fb33b1d4b5cec0d9b0ac2a8c4aabbd16b666dd"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-26T02:21:53.370Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f45252e8e8358ffe097d038b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-26T02:21:53.369Z","author":"pi-glm","text":"Two new tests close the class: a property matrix proving outerProofTime keeps the unscaled floor at scale 0.4, is unchanged at 1, preserves 3x deep budgets, and never drops below testTime for a 1..250,000 ms sweep; and an adversarial runner that re-runs the whole file as a child at explicit scale 0.005 with a reentrancy-guard env and asserts the child still passes (NODE_TEST_CONTEXT must be dropped from the child env — an empty string makes node:test skip file execution). Revert proofs in disposable copies at default scale: reverting only line 43 to testTime failed the adversarial test with child ETIMEDOUT (3 pass/1 fail); reverting only line 23 failed the adversarial test (the instrumented child outlives the 50 ms watchdog); removing the outerProofTime floor failed both new tests (value mismatch at 0.4 plus child ETIMEDOUT) while the two pre-existing tests stayed green in every case. The restored implementation passed 4/4 after each revert, plus 4/4 under V8 coverage, 4/4 at deep scale 3, and the packed consumers passed 45/45 after a build."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-26T02:21:53.370Z"}],"before_hash":"a2e41fcc088a85943f279d56d8649fd4fd07015818659aa90f48b3fe62195516","after_hash":"0c1ab7b1738538dd1e2a317402421bc5344c54847e5c68549417889c453d5f6a","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b39689843bdff33641fa7475680796a99be16b8eada094883dd8c10d3fbaa809"}
